  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "While playing in the plains, Chef found a point AAA with coordinates (X,Y)(X, Y)(X,Y).\n\nChef is interested in finding the number of straight lines passing through the point AAA such that their intercepts on both axes are **positive integers**.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nFirst and only line of input contains two integers XXX and YYY - the coordinates of the point AAA.\n\n\nOutput Format\n\nFor each test case, print an integer - the number of lines satisfying the given conditions.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤X≤10121 \\leq X \\leq 10^{12}1≤X≤1012",
      "1≤Y≤10121 \\leq Y \\leq 10^{12}1≤Y≤1012"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "3 2",
        "output": "4",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nThere are 444 lines satisfying all the conditions. These lines are:"
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_2",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "1 2",
        "output": "2",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nThere are 222 such lines, which are :"
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_3",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "28 206",
        "output": "16",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nThere are 161616 such lines."
      }
    ]
  },
